---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CTABanner from '../components/CTABanner.astro';
import JsonLd from '../components/JsonLd.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/schema';

const breadcrumb = breadcrumbSchema([
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'About', path: '/about' },
]);
---

<Layout
  title="About — InnovAItion Edge"
  description="A small, founder-led Microsoft 365 solutions provider based in Coimbatore. We modernize the M365 workplace with AI agents, custom apps, and Power Platform automation."
  canonical="/about"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <JsonLd schema={breadcrumb} />
  </Fragment>

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>A small team betting hard on the Microsoft&nbsp;365 substrate.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        InnovAItion Edge is a Coimbatore-based Microsoft 365 solutions
        provider. We exist for one reason: to make the M365 platforms
        enterprises already own — SharePoint, Teams, Power Platform,
        Azure AI — actually deliver on the promise the license implies.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section belief-section" aria-labelledby="belief-h">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">What we believe</p>
      <h2 id="belief-h">Depth on one stack beats surface on ten.</h2>
      <div class="belief-body">
        <p>
          Most enterprise IT estates are running a zoo of SaaS tools bolted
          on top of an M365 tenant that costs a fortune and does 20% of what
          it can. Every new productivity problem gets solved by procuring
          another tool, wiring it into SSO, and adding it to the mental
          load of the people who have to use it.
        </p>
        <p>
          We think the interesting move is the opposite one: to take the
          Microsoft platform seriously — SharePoint as a real content
          system, Teams as a real application surface, Power Platform as a
          real automation runtime, Azure AI as a real agent platform — and
          push it to its limits. When you do, most of the "we need a new
          SaaS for X" pressure quietly disappears.
        </p>
        <p>
          That is what we ship. Every engagement is aimed at replacing
          spreadsheet-and-email operational drag with something that lives
          natively where your people already work.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section founder-section" aria-labelledby="founder-h">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">Founder note</p>
      <h2 id="founder-h">Who you are actually talking to</h2>
      <div class="founder-body">
        <p>
          I am <strong>Naveen Prasath Selvaraj</strong>, the founder and
          builder here. Before starting InnovAItion Edge I spent years
          embedded in enterprise Microsoft 365 estates — the good, the bad,
          and the frankly-inherited. That work is the reason this company
          exists in the shape it does.
        </p>
        <p>
          When you contact us, you get me. Not a scheduling assistant, not
          a sales development rep, not a solution architect with a slide
          deck. If we agree to work together, I am one of the people
          actually building it. That is deliberate — it is the only way to
          honestly claim the "ship in weeks, not quarters" pitch.
        </p>
        <p>
          I am based in Coimbatore, India, and work with clients globally
          across time zones. Reply hours are Mon–Fri, 09:00–18:00 IST.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section stance-section" aria-labelledby="stance-h">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="stance-head">
        <p class="section-eyebrow">Our stance</p>
        <h2 id="stance-h">Three things we will not do</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="stance-grid">
        <div class="stance">
          <h3>Ship a slide-deck engagement</h3>
          <p>
            Every project ends with running software your team is using —
            not a PDF and a handover. If you want an assessment, there are
            better firms for that.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="stance">
          <h3>Chase every AI trend</h3>
          <p>
            We build Azure AI + Copilot Studio because they live in the
            same tenant, same permission model, same identity as everything
            else we ship. We will not add a third vector database if
            Azure AI Search already fits.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="stance">
          <h3>Grow into an account layer</h3>
          <p>
            We stay small on purpose. The moment there is an account
            manager between you and the person writing the code, the
            engagement stops working the way it works today.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTABanner
    heading="Curious if we are the right fit?"
    subheading="A 30-minute discovery call is enough to know. We will tell you honestly if we are — and if not, where to look."
    ctaLabel="Book a discovery call"
  />
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding: var(--space-20) 0 var(--space-12);
    background:
      radial-gradient(ellipse at 20% 0%, rgba(244, 128, 39, 0.08), transparent 60%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, #fff, var(--color-surface-alt));
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-primary-700);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }

  .page-hero h1 {
    max-width: 22ch;
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: var(--fs-lg);
    color: var(--color-ink-500);
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin: var(--space-6) 0 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .section-eyebrow {
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-primary-700);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
  }

  .belief-section h2,
  .founder-section h2 {
    max-width: 22ch;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .belief-body p,
  .founder-body p {
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    color: var(--color-ink-500);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  .belief-body p:last-child,
  .founder-body p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .founder-body strong {
    color: var(--color-ink-900);
  }

  .founder-section {
    background: var(--color-surface-alt);
    border-block: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  /* Stance */
  .stance-head {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
  }

  .stance-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .stance h3 {
    font-size: var(--fs-lg);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
  }

  .stance p {
    color: var(--color-ink-500);
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 780px) {
    .stance-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-6);
    }
  }
</style>
